{"c":[{"id":"56870ee32e779000","sum":"B17-B18: event cards judge only the last finished sentence (test bodies end with it, arrive as a change); Balanced allows 4 offers/hour (use eager); typed About values fill only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (16/20 held-out, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1148a14e8f8ea414","sum":"B17 socket tests: an event card judges only the last finished sentence, so a body ends with it and arrives as a change (empty first); Balanced allows 4 offers an hour, so a test needing a fifth sends level eager first.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-a560fe18d0d7ba87","text":"Balanced allows 4 offers an hour (settings.ts LEVELS): a socket test that needs a fifth pop-up sends settings level eager first, or the gate silently holds it (B17).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0bc8adb9f0371420","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev picks typed About Name/Email at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; prompt rewordings did not help. Such a value fills only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16 of 20, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-ec0243a8194ed7a7","text":"Live Jev picks a typed About Name/Email in both asks but at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 fill cutoff, on standalone forms (B17 held-out: 1-3 of 17 filled, 0 wrong); three prompt rewordings on a dev set did not raise it (evidence/screen/b17/dev).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-3b718a56937eb180","text":"A typed About value fills only when both asks also answer the field's whose-details question as the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (fill.ts); a memory cutoff alone needed 0.6 on B18's dev set and filled 4-7 of 20, the whose question 12 of 20, held-out live 16 of 20 with 0 wrong.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"184666ae87f4b0f6","sum":"A13: ask field sits in the keyable non-activating activity panel (sendEvent takes Return/Tab/Esc/Cmd-Z); drive it with scripts/pid-keys.swift, not cua-driver. Golden line 32 now has calendar. --calendar-test without Calendar access hands off blocked tcc, no grant.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7b00489091032a4a","sum":"A13: the ask field lives in the keyable, non-activating activity list panel, whose sendEvent intercepts Return/Tab/Esc/Cmd-Z (the field editor eats Tab and Esc first). Golden protocol line 32 now has the calendar role (b610800); HelperProtocolTests compares it as is.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T195705Z-0509a06fd894e25f","text":"Caret's ask field lives in the activity list panel (OverlayPanel keyable, non-activating); Return/Tab/Esc are intercepted in the panel's sendEvent, because the field editor eats Tab and Esc before SwiftUI onKeyPress (A13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T195705Z-b2dcf80bc4cc0ac3","text":"helper/fixtures/golden/protocol.ndjson line 32 still holds the host's pre-calendar default roles; HelperProtocolTests compares it with calendar removed until the screen track rewrites the line (A13).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"028910e321e65bd9","sum":"A13: cua-driver background keys refuse Caret's own panels; drive the ask field with scripts/pid-keys.swift. reader --calendar-test without Calendar access ends the event run as handoff blocked tcc before any calendarGrant, so no revoke to assert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T195705Z-c193056a6c54a222","text":"cua-driver's background press_key/type_text refuse Caret's own panels (not in the host's AXWindows: off_space_or_ax_unresolved); drive the ask field with apps/caret/scripts/pid-keys.swift (CGEventPostToPid, executable rechecked per event) (A13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T195705Z-d51a855e42ff6461","text":"With reader --calendar-test on a Mac without Calendar access, the event run ends as handoff blocked tcc at the first calendarFind, before any calendarGrant: no grant is issued, so don't assert a revoke there (A13).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
